# Phase 19 – Shared Platform Compliance & Integration Audit

You have completed all previous implementation phases of **Munaxa Docs**.

This phase is **NOT** about adding new features.

This phase is **NOT** about redesigning the architecture.

Your task is to ensure that **Munaxa Docs fully complies with the Munaxa Shared Platform** and consumes every shared capability instead of duplicating it.

Treat the **Munaxa Platform repository as the single source of truth**.

---

# Objective

Perform a complete repository audit and, where appropriate, refactor Munaxa Docs so that it conforms to the shared platform architecture.

The goal is to make Munaxa Docs a **thin business application** that contains only document-control business logic while consuming all cross-cutting capabilities from the Platform.

---

# Source of Truth

The Platform repository is authoritative for:

* Design System
* Design Tokens
* UI Components
* Theme
* Typography
* Icons
* Layouts
* Authentication
* Authorization
* RBAC
* Permissions
* Audit Framework
* Logging
* Notifications
* Shared Configuration
* Shared Utilities
* Shared SDK
* Shared Types
* Shared Interfaces
* Shared Infrastructure
* Shared Services

If Munaxa Docs contains its own implementation of any of these without a justified reason, treat it as a compliance violation.

